# notebooks/ and docs/ ARE tracked on purpose.
#
# They are byte-identical on every rebuild (verified: two consecutive builds
# diff clean), they render directly on GitHub, and notebooks/ is the primary
# way to take the course — a fresh clone should be usable without a build
# step. Regenerate with:
#     uv run learn.py notebooks
#     uv run learn.py export docs
# Your own edits are protected: the generator skips notebooks you have
# changed unless you pass --force.

# site/ is NOT tracked. It bakes executed output into the page, so timeit
# numbers, object sizes and ids churn ~80 lines on every build, and it is
# ~1 MB. Rebuild it instead:
#     uv run learn.py site
# (If you want to publish it via GitHub Pages, delete the next line and
# accept the churn.)
site/

# your working files and progress
workspace/
.progress.json

# python / tooling
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
